  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Choral liturgy of the nineteenth-century Central European synagogue, shaped by Salomon Sulzer, cantor of the Vienna Stadttempel from 1826 and compiler of Schir Zion, and by Louis Lewandowski, music director of Berlin's synagogues, whose Kol Rinnah and Todah W'simrah set the service for cantor, four-part choir and, in Reform congregations, organ. Their harmonized settings of the traditional prayer modes spread through the choral synagogues of Germany, Austria and Eastern Europe and remain in use in Ashkenazi congregations worldwide.",
